From 74cbc33dbf77a9415e4cc6d370cb6fdad4d2ec52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Vasconcelos <Felipe.Vasconcelos@windriver.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:38:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zh-Hans: complete credential-panel, delete-confirm and
 openstack_auth coverage

Supply first-pass Simplified Chinese (zh_Hans) translations for strings
that the shipped 25.3.0 zh_Hans catalogs lack: the Identity and Settings
Credentials / User Credentials panels, the Application Credentials create
help paragraphs, the two delete-confirmation djangojs msgids used by the
confirm dialog, and five openstack_auth messages (TOTP passcode and
authentication prompts, cookie hint, system-scope switch messages),
and two messages added by StarlingX's own Horizon patches (the
auto-refresh failure notice and the protected-object delete error),
plus upstream strings on platform screens that the 25.3.0 catalogs
lack (system-scope context menu, user-credential delete actions,
locked-password message, TOTP form title, numbered pagination).
Also un-fuzzy the Role/Roles plural so the AngularJS Roles panel title
renders with upstream's own existing translation.

The Debian build compiles the shipped .po without merging the extraction
template, so these strings need explicit entries in the shipped catalogs.
The openstack_auth entries are appended to the existing catalog; the
patch modifies that file and must not create it.

The translations are an AI-assisted first pass and are not releasable
until a native-language review approves them.

Signed-off-by: Felipe Vasconcelos <Felipe.Vasconcelos@windriver.com>
